  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  instructionDatas:
  - instructionsID: 0
    conditions: []
    procedureData: To set your spawn point, point your right hand toward the floor
      and pinch your fingers. This will define where the level objects will appear.
      You can always reset your spawn point from the settings menu
    procedureEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 0}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: SpawnPointSelector, Assembly-CSharp
          m_MethodName: ResetSpawnPoint
          m_Mode: 1
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    canByPass: 1
  - instructionsID: 1
    conditions: []
    procedureData: Brilliant!! Now lets go over the things you need to know to get
      started.
    procedureEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls:
        - m_Target: {fileID: 0}
          m_TargetAssemblyTypeName: GameManager, Assembly-CSharp
          m_MethodName: SpawnCurrentLevel
          m_Mode: 3
          m_Arguments:
            m_ObjectArgument: {fileID: 0}
            m_ObjectArgumentAssemblyTypeName: UnityEngine.Object, UnityEngine
            m_IntArgument: 0
            m_FloatArgument: 0
            m_StringArgument: 
            m_BoolArgument: 0
          m_CallState: 2
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    canByPass: 1
  - instructionsID: 2
    conditions: []
    procedureData: Your Build Remote lets you toggle between Build Mode and Edit
      Mode. Use Build Mode to place platforms and support beams. Switch to Edit Mode
      when you need to remove nodes, delete existing supports or bridges.
    procedureEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    canByPass: 1
  - instructionsID: 3
    conditions: []
    procedureData: In Build Mode, make a pinch gesture with your left hand to spawn
      a node. Then, make a pinch gesture with your right hand to connect nodes forming
      bridges or support beams.
    procedureEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    canByPass: 1
  - instructionsID: 4
    conditions: []
    procedureData: Add more support beams to strengthen your bridge, weak structures
      may collapse when the car tries to cross. Build smart to avoid failure!
    procedureEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    canByPass: 1
  - instructionsID: 5
    conditions: []
    procedureData: "Keep an eye on your budget, once you exceed it, you won\u2019t
      be able to place any more supports. Plan efficiently to stay within limits
      and complete the level."
    procedureEvent:
      m_PersistentCalls:
        m_Calls: []
    clip: {fileID: 0}
    canByPass: 1
  currentInstructionID: 0
  endInstructionID: 6
